{"name":"Chewing Gum Pink","hex":"#e292b6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chewing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of chew"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act by which something is chewed on; mastication.","The consumption of (the juice from) the khat plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chewing"},{"term":"gum","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Guambiano."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The flesh around the teeth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gum"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chewing gum","blocks":[{"text":"Chewing gum is a soft, cohesive substance designed to be chewed without being swallowed. Modern chewing gum is composed of gum base, sweeteners, softeners/plasticizers, flavors, colors, and, typically, a hard or powdered polyol coating. Its texture is reminiscent of rubber because of the physical-chemical properties of its polymer, plasticizer, and resin components, which contribute to its elastic-plastic, sticky, chewy characteristics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Chewing_gum_stick.jpg/330px-Chewing_gum_stick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chewing_gum","wikidata":"Q130878"},{"title":"Chewing","blocks":[{"text":"Chewing or mastication is the process by which food is crushed and ground by the teeth. It is the first step in the process of digestion, allowing a greater surface area for digestive enzymes and bile to break down the foods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Macaca_arctoides.png/330px-Macaca_arctoides.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chewing","wikidata":"Q827742"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Fruit-Stipe-Gum-Sticks.jpg/500px-Fruit-Stipe-Gum-Sticks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Fruit-Stipe-Gum-Sticks.jpg/1280px-Fruit-Stipe-Gum-Sticks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Fruit-Stipe-Gum-Sticks.jpg/500px-Fruit-Stipe-Gum-Sticks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sticks of Fruit Stripe chewing gum","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFruit-Stipe-Gum-Sticks.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/CHICLEROSPCIQUINTANAROO001.jpg/500px-CHICLEROSPCIQUINTANAROO001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/CHICLEROSPCIQUINTANAROO001.jpg/1280px-CHICLEROSPCIQUINTANAROO001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/CHICLEROSPCIQUI